      For styling, I opted for TailwindCSS because it provides a utility-first approach allowing for rapid UI development and it is highly customisable.\n\n
      To maintain code quality and consistency, I've implemented Prettier for consistent code formatting and ESLint along with custom configs and airbnb-base config.\n\n
      I integrated DecapCMS headless CMS to manage my blog posts and portfolio content as it provides a user-friendly interface for content creation and editing, while keeping my content as part of my Git repository.\n\n
